WEBVTT

00:02.374 --> 00:04.569
Help me out here, doc,
I need a time of death.

00:04.743 --> 00:09.146
Sorry, lieutenant, but I can't give you
an official ToD until I get her on the slab.

00:10.082 --> 00:12.277
But based on hypostatic lividity...

00:13.052 --> 00:14.644
...and degree of rigor...

00:14.820 --> 00:17.288
...I'd say our cheerleader
got her pom-poms pierced...

00:17.456 --> 00:19.447
...right around halftime.

00:20.659 --> 00:22.627
- Real?
- Real.

00:24.263 --> 00:25.287
Anything else?

00:25.697 --> 00:28.097
Left-handed assailant,
used a single-edged blade.

00:28.267 --> 00:30.827
Multiple entry wounds
and defensive trauma.

00:31.003 --> 00:33.096
So how are we gonna find
this psychopath?

00:33.272 --> 00:38.608
Well, like our killer,
we'll just have to take a stab at it.

00:43.348 --> 00:44.940
That's it.

00:48.520 --> 00:50.545
So you think I'll get the part?

00:51.790 --> 00:58.195
Uh... Well, I, for one, totally buy you
as a brilliant forensic investigator.

00:58.363 --> 01:02.265
Thanks.
But I believe it's pronounced "fornesic. "

01:03.969 --> 01:06.199
What do you think, Charlie?

01:06.438 --> 01:07.803
Unbelievable.

01:08.340 --> 01:09.500
Aww.

01:09.975 --> 01:13.001
I mean, beyond belief.

01:13.178 --> 01:14.202
That's sweet.

01:14.379 --> 01:17.143
I mean, I just don't believe it.

01:17.316 --> 01:19.511
You made your point, Charlie.

01:20.352 --> 01:22.479
Do you like what I did with the glasses?

01:22.654 --> 01:26.488
On smart, off hot.

01:28.093 --> 01:30.323
My mind is just completely blown.

01:32.531 --> 01:33.998
So when are you gonna be on Tv?

01:34.166 --> 01:35.895
I have to pass the audition first.

01:36.068 --> 01:38.696
Let's not put the can't before the whores.

01:40.973 --> 01:42.406
- Horse.
- Ahem.

01:42.574 --> 01:45.737
Maybe a little.
I've been rehearsing all day.

01:49.815 --> 01:52.249
&lt;i>- What's the name of the show?
- Stiffs.&lt;/i>

01:53.218 --> 01:54.242
&lt;i>Stiffs?&lt;/i>

01:54.419 --> 01:56.011
You know, like dead bodies.

01:56.188 --> 01:58.383
Oh, right. Sure.

01:58.757 --> 02:01.123
I know what you were thinking.

02:02.427 --> 02:03.860
Well, I'd better go.

02:04.029 --> 02:07.089
The auditiors at 4
and I still have to get my tan sprayed on.

02:07.266 --> 02:08.290
Best of luck.

02:08.467 --> 02:10.367
It has nothing to do with luck, Alan.

02:10.536 --> 02:14.028
You just have to stand still
and keep your eyes and mouth closed.

02:15.107 --> 02:17.632
No, I... I meant... Never mind.

02:17.809 --> 02:19.709
- Knock them dead at the audition.
- Thanks.

02:19.878 --> 02:22.142
And thanks for lending me
your chiropractor coat.

02:22.314 --> 02:24.373
It makes me feel like a real doctor.

02:24.550 --> 02:26.279
Now you know why Alan wears it.

02:28.387 --> 02:29.911
Okay, well, tell me how it goes.

02:30.088 --> 02:31.453
I will.

02:31.623 --> 02:34.114
Oh, and by the way,
did you get the divorce papers?

02:34.293 --> 02:37.785
Not really
but my lawyer explained them to me. Bye.

02:39.631 --> 02:42.156
They need to be signed.
Kandi?

02:48.640 --> 02:49.732
Hey, what's your hurry?

02:50.342 --> 02:54.142
If she becomes a big Tv star while you're
married, she'll have to pay you alimony.

02:54.313 --> 02:56.941
Yeah, and if pigs start flying out
of my rear end...

02:57.115 --> 02:59.948
...we'll have free bacon
for the rest of our lives.

03:03.121 --> 03:05.851
I don't know that I'd eat that bacon.

03:51.670 --> 03:54.070
Isn't anybody gonna get that?

04:03.482 --> 04:06.144
- Jake?
Yeah?

04:08.587 --> 04:10.919
- What are you doing?
- Hanging posters.

04:17.963 --> 04:19.897
Did you consider using Scotch tape?

04:20.232 --> 04:22.564
It doesn't hold as well. Especially her.

04:24.870 --> 04:26.667
- Who is that?
- Raven.

04:26.838 --> 04:29.568
She's the North American
ladies' wrestling champ.

04:30.309 --> 04:31.469
Aha.

04:31.643 --> 04:34.703
All oiled up and ready...

04:35.080 --> 04:36.570
...to wrestle.

04:40.118 --> 04:42.018
Damn it, this isn't funny.

04:45.123 --> 04:47.523
Quick little bastards.

04:48.794 --> 04:50.921
&lt;i>What happened
to your Harry Potter posters?&lt;/i>

04:51.096 --> 04:52.563
I'm not a kid anymore, Dad.

04:52.731 --> 04:54.926
You don't have to be a kid
to like Harry Potter.

04:55.100 --> 04:56.465
You want it, take it.

04:57.402 --> 05:00.098
Oh, Harry. You crumpled Harry.

05:00.272 --> 05:02.433
- Do you remember when we got this?
- Nope.

05:02.607 --> 05:03.801
Oh, come on.

05:03.975 --> 05:07.843
We stood on line outside that bookstore
at midnight to get one of the first copies.

05:08.013 --> 05:10.277
You were dressed as Harry
and I was Dumbledore.

05:10.615 --> 05:11.707
Don't remember, Dad.

05:13.051 --> 05:14.075
Sure you do.

05:14.252 --> 05:17.346
You made fun of that kid
because he had a mop instead of a broom...

05:17.522 --> 05:21.083
...and he started crying
and his father punched me in the chest?

05:22.294 --> 05:23.352
No.

05:23.695 --> 05:26.289
Yeah, well, you werert the one
with the cracked rib.

05:26.832 --> 05:30.632
Anyway, what...?
What prompted you to redecorate like this?

05:31.303 --> 05:33.328
I don't know. I like cars and wrestling.

05:33.505 --> 05:35.302
And wet T-shirts, apparently.

05:36.541 --> 05:39.305
Oh, there is a wet T-shirt in that.
I hadrt noticed.

05:44.950 --> 05:46.349
Hah!

05:52.257 --> 05:53.849
Huh.

05:54.025 --> 05:55.322
Jake's redecorating.

05:55.894 --> 05:58.863
Yeah, I can see that.

05:59.064 --> 06:01.658
Oh, Raven.

06:02.401 --> 06:03.663
Those are fake, by the way.

06:03.835 --> 06:04.893
Charlie?

06:05.070 --> 06:06.537
What? He has a right to know.

06:07.038 --> 06:10.064
I'm just glad the little guy's got me to...
Wait a minute.

06:10.609 --> 06:12.372
Are those nails in my wall?

06:12.544 --> 06:14.239
Are you out of your freaking mind?

06:15.280 --> 06:16.907
- No.
- No?

06:17.082 --> 06:18.515
That's your answer? No?

06:19.918 --> 06:21.249
Yeah.

06:21.420 --> 06:23.047
Charlie. Charlie, come on. Come on.

06:23.221 --> 06:26.850
Oh, for God's sake,
these are railroad spikes.

06:27.926 --> 06:28.950
I'll putty over it.

06:29.127 --> 06:32.187
That's not plaster board, that's stucco.
You can't putty stucco.

06:32.497 --> 06:36.797
- I know, I'll fix it. Let's give him privacy.
- All right, wait, wait, wait.

06:37.903 --> 06:40.667
At least I can take one hammer
out of his hand.

06:43.909 --> 06:46.207
&lt;i>ALAN
Jake, look at Daddy. Look at Daddy.&lt;/i>

06:47.078 --> 06:48.773
&lt;i>Look at Daddy.&lt;/i>

06:48.947 --> 06:52.280
&lt;i>Ah. That's my boy. Wave at Daddy.
Yes, Daddy's over here.&lt;/i>

06:52.451 --> 06:54.442
Wasrt he adorable?

06:54.619 --> 06:55.984
Yeah.

06:56.555 --> 06:58.955
Hey, could you rewind to Judith
breast-feeding him?

07:01.893 --> 07:04.487
That was really adorable.

07:06.832 --> 07:09.926
Especially the part
where she does the old switcheroo.

07:18.243 --> 07:19.904
I miss that little boy.

07:20.078 --> 07:23.070
It seems like only yesterday,
I could hold him in one arm.

07:23.782 --> 07:26.478
He didn't weigh
more than 8 or 9 pounds.

07:26.852 --> 07:29.320
He craps more than that now.

07:34.826 --> 07:36.020
Where did the time go?

07:36.194 --> 07:38.025
I mean, his childhood is almost over...

07:38.196 --> 07:40.926
...and there's still so much stuff
I wanna do with him.

07:41.233 --> 07:43.861
- Like what?
- Well, you know, father-son stuff.

07:44.035 --> 07:48.734
I mean, pretty soon, there'll be
no more playing catch or riding bikes.

07:48.907 --> 07:51.341
Do you realize
I've never even taken him fishing...

07:51.510 --> 07:53.102
...or camping or hunting?

07:53.278 --> 07:56.372
Do you know how to fish
or camp or hunt?

07:58.149 --> 08:00.117
That's not the point.

08:00.685 --> 08:02.550
I thought we would learn together.

08:02.721 --> 08:05.121
That's good.
You and knucklehead out in the woods...

08:05.290 --> 08:07.986
...taking turns,
shooting each other in the ass.

08:13.331 --> 08:15.993
Okay, it's not so much
about hunting per se.

08:16.167 --> 08:18.897
Per se. There's an outdoorsy phrase.

08:19.437 --> 08:21.200
It's about bonding.

08:21.373 --> 08:24.831
Before you know it, he'll have no interest
in spending time with me at all.

08:25.010 --> 08:27.410
Not unless you grow boobs
and straddle a Harley.

08:30.949 --> 08:33.008
All right, it doesn't help
to whine about it.

08:33.184 --> 08:37.416
If you wanna get lost in the woods
with Jerky Gherkineimer, go do it.

08:38.857 --> 08:41.587
My life is just one big joke to you,
isn't it?

08:41.860 --> 08:44.590
Actually, it's more of a limerick.

08:46.264 --> 08:51.167
&lt;i>There once was a moron named Al
Who wanted to camp with his pal&lt;/i>

08:53.371 --> 08:56.534
Any chance you can go camping
in Nantucket?

09:04.282 --> 09:06.682
So, Charlie, where's the wife and kid?

09:06.985 --> 09:10.216
They went camping
to do some father-son bonding.

09:27.272 --> 09:31.936
And when they looked
at the door handle of the car...

09:32.978 --> 09:35.037
...there was nothing there...

09:35.380 --> 09:37.177
...but a hook.

09:38.416 --> 09:41.385
Hook? That makes no sense.

09:41.553 --> 09:42.747
Oh, I left out a part.

09:44.055 --> 09:46.114
The guy who escaped
from the insane asylum...

09:46.291 --> 09:48.919
...had lost his hand
in some kind of industrial accident.

09:49.094 --> 09:51.790
Anyway, they...
They replaced it with sharp metal hook.

09:53.164 --> 09:55.496
And it was said hook...

09:55.667 --> 09:59.262
...that was stuck
on the aforementioned door handle.

10:02.474 --> 10:04.965
Wooo-ooo-ooo.

10:05.143 --> 10:10.103
Dad, over the past three birthdays,
I've gotten $ 175 in bookstore gift cards.

10:10.281 --> 10:13.079
They're yours if we could just go home.

10:13.251 --> 10:15.082
No, no, we're... We're having fun.

10:15.253 --> 10:18.450
Hey, hey, I know. We'll sing a song.

10:24.462 --> 10:26.191
Come on. You used to love this one.

10:40.445 --> 10:41.639
Come on.

10:51.866 --> 10:54.960
Oh, come on. We had an adventure.

10:58.873 --> 11:00.431
- Dad?
- Yeah, buddy?

11:00.742 --> 11:02.004
Bite me.

11:05.780 --> 11:09.477
You'll see. Someday you and I
will look back on this weekend...

11:09.651 --> 11:12.279
...and laugh and laugh...

11:16.658 --> 11:18.353
I didn't say someday soon.

11:21.095 --> 11:24.587
Hey, come on.
I thought you liked wet T-shirts.

11:34.676 --> 11:36.041
Hey.

11:36.511 --> 11:38.035
Hey.

11:41.215 --> 11:42.341
Shut up.

11:43.985 --> 11:47.250
Oh, come on, Alan,
we both know I can't do that.

11:48.456 --> 11:52.153
What do you want me to say?
It was a bad idea? Okay, it was a bad idea.

11:52.327 --> 11:54.989
The only thing we bonded over
was our mutual discomfort...

11:55.163 --> 11:57.654
...with pooping into a coffee can.

11:58.399 --> 12:00.333
It wasrt Chock full o'Nuts, was it?

12:03.771 --> 12:05.830
Sorry, sorry. Where's Jake?

12:06.307 --> 12:09.276
He went back to his friends
in Hooterville.

12:12.413 --> 12:16.816
Well, I can't blame him.
It never rains in Hooterville.

12:18.519 --> 12:22.216
Look, Alan, seriously,
I'm sorry it didn't work out.

12:22.390 --> 12:24.858
- I know your heart was in the right place.
- Thank you.

12:25.159 --> 12:28.185
Now, I finished the limerick,
you wanna hear it?

12:30.565 --> 12:31.725
Too soon?

12:33.434 --> 12:34.458
You don't get it.

12:34.636 --> 12:37.901
You don't understand what it's like to be
a little boy's best friend...

12:38.072 --> 12:39.767
...to be someone he looks up to.

12:39.941 --> 12:42.808
Then one day, you turn around
and the person he looks up to...

12:42.977 --> 12:45.775
...is covered with baby oil
and nailed to the ceiling.

12:45.947 --> 12:48.415
Count your blessings.
There's all kinds of pictures...

12:48.583 --> 12:50.244
...that could be up there.
- I guess.

12:50.418 --> 12:52.147
It could have been the Moscow Ballet.

12:53.921 --> 12:58.415
I got it. Still, I can't help
but feel a little empty inside.

12:58.593 --> 13:01.061
Like a chapter of my life is over.

13:01.229 --> 13:03.891
So? You've still got
plenty to look forward to.

13:04.065 --> 13:07.728
You mean, besides work,
loneliness and death?

13:08.403 --> 13:09.870
Absolutely.

13:10.038 --> 13:13.474
There's memory loss.

13:15.176 --> 13:16.973
Impotence.

13:17.779 --> 13:19.610
Adult diapers.

13:21.683 --> 13:23.742
I'm all you've got, pal.

13:28.690 --> 13:33.024
That's true.
My wives are gone, my son is grown.

13:33.194 --> 13:35.458
But I'll always have you.

13:36.931 --> 13:38.592
My brother.

13:42.937 --> 13:44.632
Forever.

13:46.774 --> 13:50.039
Okay, now I was just having fun
but that was mean.

13:54.215 --> 13:56.410
Well, when will he be back?

13:56.584 --> 13:59.451
All right, tell him I called again.

13:59.620 --> 14:00.746
Boy, some agent.

14:00.922 --> 14:03.288
He never calls, he never returns my calls.

14:03.458 --> 14:06.325
I'm almost sorry I let him feel me up.

14:07.995 --> 14:10.156
Well, I guess that's showbiz.

14:10.465 --> 14:12.558
That's what he said.

14:13.768 --> 14:16.566
- Listen, Kandi...
- I thought they liked me at that audition.

14:16.738 --> 14:19.298
They had me read three times
and all the jumping jacks...

14:19.474 --> 14:21.874
- Jumping jacks?
- It's an action series, Alan.

14:22.043 --> 14:23.806
They need to know that I'm fit.

14:24.946 --> 14:26.243
Ah. Uh...

14:26.414 --> 14:29.713
Listen, Kandi, there's something
I wanted to talk to you about.

14:29.884 --> 14:32.352
If it's the divorce papers,
I haven't signed them yet.

14:32.520 --> 14:34.545
No, no, that's not why I'm here.

14:34.722 --> 14:37.350
Sweetie, do you remember
why we split up?

14:37.525 --> 14:40.551
- The big reason or all the little reasons?
- The big one.

14:40.728 --> 14:43.162
- Because there were a lot of little reasons.
- I know.

14:43.331 --> 14:45.993
- Like the way your toenails grow all crazy.
- Right.

14:46.167 --> 14:48.567
- And your ear hair and your nose hair.
- Got it.

14:48.736 --> 14:52.228
And that one long hair on your back.
Yuck.

14:52.840 --> 14:55.536
Okay, forget the little reasons,
just the big one.

14:56.010 --> 14:58.069
Yeah, you didn't wanna have a baby
and I did.

14:58.479 --> 15:00.242
Right. Well...

15:00.848 --> 15:03.476
What would you say
if I were to tell you...

15:04.118 --> 15:06.643
...that I've changed my mind about that?

15:07.588 --> 15:09.283
- Really?
- Yeah.

15:09.457 --> 15:13.917
I've just been thinking
that Jake is almost grown...

15:14.095 --> 15:16.222
...and there's still a lot of daddy
left in me.

15:17.965 --> 15:19.557
So you wanna have a baby?

15:20.067 --> 15:21.227
Yes, I do.

15:21.402 --> 15:24.200
A fresh start. A new chapter.

15:24.639 --> 15:26.573
Wow, that's a big step.

15:26.741 --> 15:29.767
Yeah. I know. I know it is.
So if you wanna think about it, I...

15:29.944 --> 15:31.775
No, that's okay. Let's make a baby.

15:32.914 --> 15:35.474
Just like that?
Don't you wanna talk about it some more?

15:35.650 --> 15:39.177
Alan, it's practically all we talked
about our entire marriage.

15:39.353 --> 15:44.347
Baby, baby, toenails, baby, ear hair,
baby, how clocks work, baby.

15:46.994 --> 15:49.326
So you really wanna do this?

15:50.164 --> 15:51.563
Do what?

15:54.435 --> 15:56.335
You see, if you use tape...

15:56.504 --> 16:00.941
...it's much easier to rotate in new posters
when these ones stop working for you.

16:01.542 --> 16:03.772
I don't think that's gonna happen.

16:03.945 --> 16:05.537
Trust me, after a while...

16:05.713 --> 16:09.342
...these beautiful eyes are gonna be filled
with judgment and condemnation.

16:09.984 --> 16:12.248
What are you talking about?

16:12.653 --> 16:14.951
Okay, maybe that was just me.

16:16.157 --> 16:19.957
Anyway, you're lucky your dad
lets you hang posters like this.

16:20.127 --> 16:21.253
I guess.

16:21.762 --> 16:23.787
- Does your mother let you?
- No way.

16:24.098 --> 16:26.965
So, what do you got at her house,
a secret stash of magazines?

16:27.468 --> 16:30.960
&lt;i>Just one.
Playboy, 1998, the Christmas issue.&lt;/i>

16:31.305 --> 16:33.000
God bless Hugh Hefner, huh?

16:33.174 --> 16:35.904
God bless Kimberly Macadoo
from Portland, oregon.

16:36.077 --> 16:37.874
Born March 4th, 1979.

16:38.045 --> 16:42.675
Turn-ons: Sunshine and goatees.
Turn-offs: Judgmental people and war.

16:43.618 --> 16:45.609
You gotta love a chick
who doesn't like war.

16:46.621 --> 16:48.213
Tape me.

16:49.123 --> 16:51.455
Hey, Uncle Charlie,
could you do me a favor?

16:51.959 --> 16:56.521
If it's the favor I'm thinking of,
not until you're 18 and not in my house.

16:57.198 --> 17:00.031
- What?
- Nothing. Nothing. What do you need?

17:00.534 --> 17:04.061
Could you get my dad to lay off
the father-son stuff? It's kind of lame.

17:04.672 --> 17:07.971
Lame? You think it's lame your father
cares so much about you...

17:08.142 --> 17:10.770
...and wants nothing more
than to be a part of your life?

17:10.945 --> 17:12.310
Yeah.

17:13.514 --> 17:16.642
Look, you gotta understand
what your father's going through.

17:16.817 --> 17:17.841
What do you mean?

17:18.686 --> 17:21.712
Okay, here's the deal.

17:22.456 --> 17:25.550
Your father has reached
a very difficult age.

17:25.726 --> 17:27.853
It's confusing
and a little bit scary for him.

17:28.029 --> 17:29.326
Scary how?

17:30.231 --> 17:32.722
Well, first of all, his body's changing.

17:32.900 --> 17:34.561
- Really?
- Oh, yeah.

17:34.735 --> 17:37.101
Hair is growing
where it's never grown before.

17:38.406 --> 17:39.998
That is scary.

17:40.174 --> 17:42.199
- And then there's the hormones.
- Hormones?

17:42.376 --> 17:45.777
Yep. Your father is running out of them.

17:46.914 --> 17:48.074
That sounds bad.

17:48.249 --> 17:51.878
No, no, it's just a perfectly natural part
of growing old, Jake.

17:52.053 --> 17:55.819
- Is it happening to you?
- No, no. No, no.

17:56.824 --> 18:00.191
My point is that your father
is going through this phase...

18:00.361 --> 18:02.625
...and you have to be patient
and understanding.

18:03.130 --> 18:05.189
So he's gonna wanna go camping again?

18:06.267 --> 18:08.792
Probably not in this lifetime.

18:09.670 --> 18:12.867
But you might have to play catch with him
or something.

18:13.274 --> 18:14.605
Guess I could do that.

18:15.042 --> 18:16.634
Attaboy.

18:16.811 --> 18:19.575
All right, well,
I'm glad we had this little talk. Ahem.

18:20.748 --> 18:22.409
I'm gonna go get hammered.

18:39.900 --> 18:43.063
Hello, ladies, I'm Harry Potter.

18:46.941 --> 18:49.205
- Is there anything special we have to do?
- Oh, no.

18:49.377 --> 18:52.574
It's a regular sex but without
the last-minute fumbling for a condom.

18:52.747 --> 18:57.013
Oh, okay. But I still get all the rest
of the fumbling, right?

18:57.818 --> 18:59.752
I prefer to call that foreplay.

19:02.323 --> 19:03.790
Hold on.

19:04.358 --> 19:05.620
Hello?

19:05.793 --> 19:07.055
This is she.

19:07.228 --> 19:09.560
Uh-huh. Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

19:09.730 --> 19:11.561
Hold on a sec.

19:13.768 --> 19:15.668
Here, we're divorced.

19:16.337 --> 19:18.498
Okay, I'm back. You were saying?

19:18.672 --> 19:21.436
Really? I got the part?

19:21.609 --> 19:23.304
Thank you so much.

19:23.477 --> 19:26.275
Thank you, thank you, thank you.

19:26.447 --> 19:27.880
Alan, I got the part.

19:28.049 --> 19:30.449
Oh. Oh, that's terrific. Congratulations.

19:30.618 --> 19:33.519
Whoa, whoa, whoa, put that thing away.

19:34.255 --> 19:36.086
- But I thought...
- oh, please.

19:36.257 --> 19:39.021
Nobody wants to see a pregnant
"fornesic" investigator.

19:43.831 --> 19:46.629
Hey, can we still do it with a condom?

19:51.539 --> 19:54.303
Hey, Dad, after this,
wanna go play catch?

19:55.476 --> 19:58.001
- It's dark out.
- Okay.

19:58.179 --> 20:00.010
I tried.

20:02.016 --> 20:05.577
&lt;i>Help me out here, doc. I need
a time of death for our little cheerleader.&lt;/i>

20:05.753 --> 20:09.348
&lt;i>I can't give you an official TOD
until I get her on the slab.&lt;/i>

20:09.523 --> 20:12.492
&lt;i>But based on hypostatic lividity
and degree of rigor...&lt;/i>

20:12.660 --> 20:15.925
&lt;i>...I'd say our cheerleader got
her pom-poms pierced around halftime.&lt;/i>

20:16.097 --> 20:17.121
&lt;i>Anything else?&lt;/i>

20:17.298 --> 20:19.596
&lt;i>Left-handed assailant,
used a single-edged blade.&lt;/i>

20:19.767 --> 20:22.167
&lt;i>Multiple entry wounds
and defensive trauma.&lt;/i>

20:22.336 --> 20:24.304
&lt;i>So how are we gonna find
this psychopath?&lt;/i>

20:24.472 --> 20:29.603
&lt;i>Well, like our killer,
we'll just have to take a stab at it.&lt;/i>

20:37.118 --> 20:39.609
Unbelievable.

20:41.155 --> 20:42.349
Yeah.

20:42.990 --> 20:44.389
They're real, you know.

20:49.563 --> 20:51.793
I know. I was married to her.

20:51.966 --> 20:53.661
Oh, yeah.

20:53.968 --> 20:56.027
Dog.

21:05.045 --> 21:07.946
You know what? I'll be in my room.

21:16.390 --> 21:18.984
So when are you guys going fishing?
